      "route_ok": true,
      "correct": true,
      "hit_at_5": true,
      "citation_precision": 0.5,
      "mode": "hybrid",
      "answer": "They selected sinusoidal positional encodings because they believed the fixed sinusoids would let the model **easily learn to attend by relative positions** \u2013 for any fixed offset\u202f\\(k\\), the encoding at position\u202f\\(pos+k\\) can be expressed as a linear function of the encoding at\u202f\\(pos\\)\u202f[1].  Experiments also showed that this choice gave results essentially identical to learned embeddings, confirming its adequacy [1][2].",
      "route_got": "document_question",
      "latency": 0.96,
